oxes × 2 SF each). Our 24 SF is within range but uses fewer, larger boxes. If boxes are smaller (1' × 1' = 1 SF each) and there are more of them (10-13), total would be 10-13 SF instead.\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"Box size assumption is critical — could range from 1 SF to 6 SF each\",\n        \"Keynote count may underrepresent actual boxes if some are not individually keynoted\",\n        \"Floor patching required — coordinate with Item 24 (Repair/Patch Subflooring)\",\n        \"MEP coordination required per keynote\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_number\": 22,\n      \"description\": \"Remove Interior Glazing\",\n      \"quantity\": 2,\n      \"unit\": \"EA\",\n      \"measurement_method\": \"Identified keynote for interior glazing removal (remove window frame and wired glass in its entirety, prepare opening to receive new fire-rated wall) on DM-100.00. Found approximately 2 keynote locations along interior corridor partitions — these are borrowed-light or fire-rated vision panels between rooms and corridor.\",\n      \"sheets_used\": [\"part3/page-10\"],\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"assumptions\": [\n        \"Each keynote bubble = 1 interior glazing assembly (frame + wired glass)\",\n        \"Located at corridor partition walls\",\n        \"Opening to be infilled with new fire-rated wall per keynote\"\n      ],\n      \"cross_check\": \"Task packets estimated 2 EA. Consistent with our count. Interior borrowed lights in hospital dental suites are typically limited to a few corridor-facing locations.\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"Wired glass = fire-rated assembly — maintain fire separation during construction\",\n        \"Opening infill with new fire-rated wall is separate scope from removal\",\n        \"Could be up to 4 if additional locations obscured by image resolution\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total_items\": 12,\n    \"high_confidence_items\": 0,\n    \"medium_confidence_items\": 5,\n    \"low_confidence_items\": 7,\n    \"overall_note\": \"Image resolution significantly limited ability to read small keynote numbers precisely. Keynote descriptions were matched to item descriptions rather than relying solely on bubble numbers. All quantities should be verified against original high-resolution drawings or PDF. Partition LF is the highest-value estimate and should be prioritized for verification.\"\n  }\n}\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":5506,"cacheRead":34177,"cacheWrite":753,"totalTokens":40437,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.13765,"cacheRead":0.0170885,"cacheWrite":0.00470625,"total":0.15944975}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1769809130005}}
